## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical API design for client resilience and caching.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotency in POST; client-side cache keys; offline mode handling; end-to-end testing strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
class CcaClientCache {
  // simple in-memory cache for demo
  constructor(ttl=60000) {
    this.ttl = ttl; this.store = new Map();
  }
  get(key){ const v=this.store.get(key); if(!v) return null; if(Date.now()-v.t > this.ttl) { this.store.delete(key); return null; } return v.value; }
  set(key, value){ this.store.set(key, {value, t: Date.now()}); }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test offline support and cache eviction?
- How would you handle multi-device sync for the same user?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a beginner grasp of privacy, fairness, and simple DP-like smoothing in a real API. It requires concrete endpoint design and data fields, plus a practical test plan.

## Key Concepts
- Locale-aware weighting
- Regional underrepresentation handling
- Laplace smoothing basics
- Privacy via hashed IDs
- Deterministic scoring for given inputs

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeScore(base, localeW, regionBias, samples, eps, delta) {
  let s = base + localeW - regionBias;
  if (samples < 50) {
    s = (s * (samples) + eps) / (samples + 1);
  }
  return Math.max(0, Math.min(100, s));
}
```

